timeshift-recovery (1.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: provision a bootable Timeshift recovery environment.
  * Builds a minimal environment with mmdebstrap against the host's own apt
    sources, so it always matches the installed release and architecture, and
    mirrors the host's linux-firmware packages for correct hardware support.
  * Places the payload on a dedicated partition when there is unallocated
    space, and otherwise on the root filesystem; the boot path is identical
    either way, so upgrades do not branch.
  * Adds a GRUB entry with --hotkey=r, so pressing R at startup boots straight
    into recovery. The boot screen is otherwise unchanged.
  * Re-provisions automatically via a dpkg trigger on the timeshift binaries,
    handing off to a systemd unit that waits for the dpkg lock rather than
    re-provisioning inside the transaction.

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:50:00 -0400
